i've got a game on the go with a Female Elven Wizard that is going so
well i'm almost scared to play it for all the YASDs that are lingering
just around the corner.

I explored down to the oracle without anything out of the ordinary
happening (aside from finding a huge surplus scrolls of enchant armor
and weapon when clearing out a bookstore, which i promptly used,
perhaps unwisely).Then i decided to double back and explore the mines.

There was a close call with a fire ant on Mines lvl 2 (i think i was
only XP 7 at the time) but i survived it. Found and ID'd a wand of poly
on mines lvl3.

My real luck came in Mine Town, though. I came across a bones file
(Here lies Darren, killed by a vampire) with a magic marker. Took care
of the vampire with judicious wand of magic missilling. I then promptly
blanked my blessed spellbook of force bult in the fountain and tried my
luck at writing a spellbook of identify.

worked on the first try!

so i locked myself in a shop with all my stuff and all Darren's stuff
and just kept casting identify over and over (with an 83% chance of
fail). Turned out Darren was also toting around a bag of holding,
scroll of charging and a magic lamp (all cursed). So  diluted some
potions in the fountain, prayed to anhur and blesssed first a scroll of
RC and then the freshly uncursed lamp. Exploring the other shops I
found gauntlets of power (never seen them before) and a second magic
lamp(!).

So I used my first lamp to wish for SDSM. I also had enough gold to
make one good offer to the priest. So all told, my AC is now down to
-15.

Not quite sure what to do next, I decided to take my first stab at
polypiling. piled up all my spellbooks and all my rings and zapped the
poly wand a couple of times. Came out of it with Spellbooks of
Fireball, Magic Missile and Charm Monster! Sure those spells will come
in handy later.

I also (entirely by accident) caught my kitten Cinders in one of those
poly blasts, turning him into an Energy Vortex. I felt bad at first,
but he seems to be having a grand old time sucking things up and
shocking them.

Cinders the Vortex and I just finished clearing out the bottom of the
mine and now (at XP lvl 12) I'm psyching myself up for the plunge down
into the deeper parts of the maze. I think I might skip sokoban (since
i already have reflection and a BoH.

I've referenced the item spoilers, but have avoided for the most part
the monster and level spoilers, so i'm not really sure what i'm heading
